      "writtenOn": "2019-07-23T22:23:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These file names are all so cryptic. Less abbreviated names help more developers get involved. How about usbc_*? e.g. usbc_state_machine.o.\n\nWe should also consider hosting all these under a sub-directory (e.g. common/usbc).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "60701cebfe256f8184c0a784d2f95e7ff5d9831f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1bad4254_a1aa2d0f",
        "filename": "common/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-24T20:30:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not apposed to changing the names but anyone working on TypeC/PD should know what these acronyms are because the spec uses them. Plus, some of the names would be quite long: CTVPD - charge_through_vconn_powered_device.",
      "parentUuid": "45350d3c_b7d0fa27",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "60701cebfe256f8184c0a784d2f95e7ff5d9831f",
