      "writtenOn": "2019-07-24T20:30:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Type-C spec. does not use a prefix when naming states but the PD spec. does: prl_tx_phy_layer_reset, pe_frs_snk_src_source_on, rch_report_error to list a few. To be consistent, I thought I\u0027d add the tc_ prefix to the typec states.\n\nAlso the protocol layer file contains several different state machines and the prefix helps to distinguish the states machines",
      "parentUuid": "4dde59a7_6a04f444",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 0,
